{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6715316","formula":"C₁₄H₂₃NO₃","hill":"C14H23NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":23.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"MEE"},"descriptions":{"en":"MEE, also known as 2-methoxy-4,5-diethoxyamphetamine or as TMA2-4,5-DiEtO, is a chemical compound of the phenethylamine, amphetamine, and DOx families related to the psychedelic drug TMA-2. It is the analogue of TMA-2 in which the methoxy groups at the 4 and 5 positions have been replaced with ethoxy groups. In his book PiHKAL (Phenethylamines I Have Known and Loved), Alexander Shulgin lists MEE's dose as greater than 4.6 mg orally and its duration as unknown."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":44719591,"mass":253.34,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCOC1=C(C=C(C(=C1)CC(C)N)OC)OCC","inchikey":"LKJRFMXILZHUHU-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(4,5-diethoxy-2-methoxyphenyl)propan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"44719591","atoms":41,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.881,"y":2.356,"z":0.154,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.853,"y":-1.647,"z":0.825,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.668,"y":0.97,"z":0.356,"el":"O"},{"x":4.709,"y":-1.634,"z":-0.245,"el":"N"},{"x":2.842,"y":-0.301,"z":0.631,"el":"C"},{"x":3.285,"y":-1.332,"z":-0.423,"el":"C"},{"x":1.375,"y":0.048,"z":0.557,"el":"C"},{"x":0.966,"y":1.36,"z":0.321,"el":"C"},{"x":0.425,"y":-0.959,"z":0.726,"el":"C"},{"x":3.074,"y":-0.835,"z":-1.853,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.934,"y":-0.654,"z":0.659,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.344,"y":0.658,"z":0.423,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.394,"y":1.665,"z":0.254,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.81,"y":-2.73,"z":-0.102,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.14,"y":1.535,"z":-0.866,"el":"C"},{"x":1.374,"y":3.668,"z":-0.083,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.204,"y":-3.299,"z":-0.26,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.584,"y":1.13,"z":-1.072,"el":"C"},{"x":3.037,"y":-0.695,"z":1.639,"el":"H"},{"x":3.466,"y":0.597,"z":0.544,"el